Pins Stage 2 reviewer Bug B (false negative, reproduced independently by the dispatcher): the script's only agent( call is opened ("agent({") but never closed with "})" before EOF. A scanner that only evaluates a block when it sees the closing marker never evaluates this block at all -- silent allow of an unambiguous unpinned call (no model: key appears anywhere in the fragment that was ever typed). The correct contract must flush and evaluate whatever was collected for an open block at EOF, rather than discarding it, and must deny here (no model: pin is present, and none ever could appear since the script ends mid-call) -- naming the offending call via the fragment "never closed block probe".
